<p>Mhm. This isn't doing it for me, unfortunately. You've got parts that are funny (dado and past!Foundation), and they clash massively with the overall tone of the thing. I understand it's meant to be a lot of severely different universes, but it reads like a parody of the multiverse concept, where everything's got it's own clear 'theme'. And I wouldn't mind that if you embraced the silliness, but despite your jokes you still seem to be shooting for something big and serious, and it just misses the mark. Technologically it's very well-done, but story-wise it just has a lot of jarring themes and clashing tones, and kinda&#8230; leaves a lot go be desired, on the narrative front.</p>
